@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Introduction to Infrastructure as Code (IaC)";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is a **modern approach** to managing and provisioning IT infrastructure through machine-readable definition files, rather than manual processes.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is Infrastructure as Code (IaC)?</h2>
        <p>Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is a methodology where **infrastructure provisioning and management** (such as servers, databases, networking) are automated through code instead of manual configurations.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Ensures **consistency** across different environments.</li>
            <li>Automates **infrastructure deployment and updates**.</li>
            <li>Reduces **human errors and configuration drift**.</li>
            <li>Improves **scalability and disaster recovery**.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/iac-diagram.png" alt="Infrastructure as Code Concept" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Infrastructure as Code automates provisioning and management.</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Types of IaC</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>**Declarative IaC:** Defines **desired state**, and the system makes the necessary changes (e.g., Terraform, ARM templates).</li>
                <li>**Imperative IaC:** Specifies **commands step-by-step** to reach the desired state (e.g., Ansible, PowerShell DSC).</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Benefits of Using IaC</h2>
        <p>Implementing Infrastructure as Code in Azure DevOps provides multiple advantages:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>**Version Control:** Store infrastructure configurations in source control (Git, Azure Repos).</li>
            <li>**Automation:** Reduce deployment time with CI/CD pipelines.</li>
            <li>**Reproducibility:** Deploy identical environments for dev, test, and production.</li>
            <li>**Security & Compliance:** Ensure consistent security policies through automated enforcement.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>How to Implement IaC in Azure DevOps</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to set up Infrastructure as Code using Azure DevOps:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Define Infrastructure:</strong> Use ARM Templates, Terraform, or Bicep for infrastructure definition.</li>
            <li><strong>Store in Source Control:</strong> Keep IaC files in **Azure Repos** or **GitHub**.</li>
            <li><strong>Configure CI/CD Pipeline:</strong> Automate infrastructure deployment using Azure Pipelines.</li>
            <li><strong>Deploy and Monitor:</strong> Continuously apply infrastructure updates through DevOps processes.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Example YAML Pipeline for IaC Deployment</h4>
            <pre>
stages:
- stage: DeployInfrastructure
  displayName: 'Deploy Infrastructure as Code'
  jobs:
  - job: TerraformApply
    steps:
    - task: TerraformTaskV2
      inputs:
        provider: 'azurerm'
        command: 'apply'
        workingDirectory: '$(Build.SourcesDirectory)/infra'
            </pre>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/iac-deployment.png" alt="IaC Deployment in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Example of Infrastructure Deployment in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Best Practices for IaC</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Use **modular IaC templates** for reusability.</li>
            <li>Implement **code reviews and approvals** before deploying infrastructure changes.</li>
            <li>Enforce **role-based access control (RBAC)** for secure deployments.</li>
            <li>Integrate **automated testing** to validate infrastructure changes before deployment.</li>
            <li>Use **infrastructure state locking** to prevent conflicts in deployments.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Infrastructure as Code (IaC) simplifies infrastructure provisioning, reduces errors, and enhances consistency across environments. Integrating IaC with Azure DevOps enables **scalable, repeatable, and secure infrastructure deployments**.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **ARM Templates vs Terraform** to choose the best IaC tool for your infrastructure needs.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-end mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("ARMvsTerraform", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: ARM Templates vs Terraform &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>
